` "eu-oaz72.175: a wrapper function whose frame holds the list head while a
   closed `+` lambda is threaded through a strict fold must not pin the list.
   Deliberately written with `if` and a `.( )` tail, against docs/eucalypt-style.md:
   the `l nil? then(...)` form pins the list by a separate route that closed
   bindings do not reach (11,256 blocks in source-prelude mode), so it cannot
   gate this fix. `.result` would add an update frame per level instead."
fs(op, i, l): if(l nil?, i, { a: op(i, l head) }.(seq(a, fs(op, a, l tail))))

c3(l): fs(+, 0, l)

x: range(0, 200000) c3
